    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="cr_d18">

                <pb facs="cr_d18-1" n="1" xml:id="cr_d18-1"/>

                <head>CR–18. Telegram from the Secretary of State to the Embassy in Costa
                        Rica<anchor n="1" xml:id="cr_d18-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1959-12-04T20:15:00-05:00">December 4, 1959,
                            8:15 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>180. For Ambassador Willauer. Treasury decision United Fruit reallocation profile
                    for tax purposes provides 60–40 division favor <pb facs="0519" n="431"
                        type="typeset" xml:id="pg431"/> Costa Rica, effective January 1, 1958,
                    informing Echandi this decision:<anchor n="2" xml:id="cr_d18-f2"/> (1) strongly
                    recommend he accept ruling as decision made in an equitable and fair manner
                    after careful consideration; (2) stress increase in allocation obtained by
                    strong efforts on part of State and UFCO; and (3) GOCR should deal directly with
                    United Fruit hereafter on this matter. Also, remind Echandi this information
                    being given him through diplomatic channels in accordance Pres. Eisenhower’s
                    letter.</p>
                <p>Copy of Decision will be forwarded Embassy as soon as available; sent UFCO Boston
                        yesterday.<anchor n="3" xml:id="cr_d18-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Herter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#cr_d18-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="cr_d18-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 811.05118/12–459. Official Use Only;
                    Niact. Drafted by Taylor and signed by Stewart.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#cr_d18-f2" n="2" xml:id="cr_d18-f2-content">
                <p>Documentation on Willauer’s informing Echandi of this decision was not found in
                    Department of State files.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#cr_d18-f3" n="3" xml:id="cr_d18-f3-content">
                <p>A copy of the letter to Baggett from Dana Latham, Commissioner of Internal
                    Revenue, December, 3, is in OAP Files, Lot 64 D 66, “United Fruit Company: Costa
                    Rica, 1959.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
